#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0147 expect=noViolation domain=DM
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when Exposure (EX) records are present for a subject, but the Subject Reference End Date/Time (RFXENDTC) in the Demographics (DM) domain does not equal the latest Exposure Start Date/Time (EXSTDTC) or the latest Exposure End Date/Time (EXENDTC) in the EX domain for that subject.
#note "Pins the deliberate ASYMMETRY of the missing_values authoring: only $max_ex_exendtc declares `indeterminate`; $max_ex_exstdtc keeps the default `skip`. Subject 1015's first exposure has a BLANK EXSTDTC, so under `skip` the latest EXSTDTC is 2014-01-10, RFXENDTC matches it, and the rule stays silent. Declaring `indeterminate` on the EXSTDTC extreme as well would leave the rule with no surviving acceptance branch and it would fire here -- which is why this scenario exists. EXENDTC is populated on both rows, so the declared extreme cannot influence the verdict and only the EXSTDTC disposition can flip this file."
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFXENDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Last Study Treatment"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | 2014-01-10
---

dataset EX label=Exposure
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col EXENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Treatment"
col EXSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Treatment"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | EX | 01-701-1015 | 2014-01-16 |
CDISCPILOT01 | EX | 01-701-1015 | 2014-01-16 | 2014-01-10
---
